{
  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.5266 acc / 0.5104 F1, a clear ~4% gain over the RNA-only baseline (config_001, 0.4849). This confirms that image features add value, but we have no information on whether the simple concat fusion is optimal or whether a learned weighted fusion could further improve the combination. Question tested: config_017 is an isolated change from config_016—only the fusion strategy shifts from concat to weighted—so it cleanly measures whether the fusion mechanism matters at this stage. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is the most controlled comparison available, changing exactly one variable, so the result is interpretable without confounding. (2) The fusion choice is a foundational design decision that propagates to every subsequent multimodal configuration (multiprofile, different encoders); knowing whether weighted > concat now prevents wasting budget on suboptimal fusion variants later. (3) If weighted fusion yields a meaningful gain, it signals that the combination mechanism is a lever worth exploring further; if it does not, we can confidently fix concat and redirect budget toward higher-uncertainty questions like multiprofile aggregation or alternative RNA encoders."
}

